{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793734704,"nonce":"588mMt5+ed5/Ej1aIaw5Z3joqwg=","message":"Implemented in 4d5d8b4 and 9d0a6bd; browser bundles fcdca2f and d27007b are deployed to staging. The browser editor header shows GitHub sign-in when anonymous, or the account login and an outlined sign-out icon when authenticated. Popup sign-in updates the header through safe account.changed bridge events; no tokens or CSRF values are broadcast. A pending header sign-in can be cancelled. Sign-out refreshes CSRF, shows loading feedback, and waits for the existing Save and Sign Out guard when files are dirty. Account checks run after mounting and stop polling when complete; subscriptions and owned sign-in attempts are cleaned up. Eleven targeted browser-agent checks pass. Native account interactions pass in light/dark at widths 480 and 1280, including failure/retry, null-state changes, cancellation and disposal. Full workbench checks pass in both themes, including top-right placement and dirty-file sign-out protection. WASM and native session release builds pass. Final staging WASM is 38,945,038 bytes; R2 read-back verifies exact bytes/hashes. Browser visual verification was limited by Chrome capture/window focus and stopped while the user was actively configuring GitHub. No real account was signed out by automation, no GitHub App settings were changed, and code/tracker refs were not pushed.","files":null}]}